From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:05:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: Take the VM context lock killably when
 mapping

A process blocked on the VM context lock behind a stuck holder stayed in
D state, its GPU memory pinned until a reboot (a Firefox thread in
__pvr_vm_map, 340 MiB). Take the lock killably so such a process can be
killed and its memory freed.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_vm.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_vm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_vm.c
index acef3197790a..03254d5d1a0a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_vm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_vm.c
@@ -765,7 +765,16 @@ __pvr_vm_map(struct pvr_vm_context *vm_ctx, struct pvr_gem_object *pvr_obj,
 
 	pvr_gem_object_get(pvr_obj);
 
-	mutex_lock(&vm_ctx->lock);
+	/*
+	 * Killable: a process blocked here behind a stuck lock holder can still be
+	 * killed, which closes its files and frees its memory, instead of staying in
+	 * D state with its GPU memory pinned until a reboot.
+	 */
+	err = mutex_lock_killable(&vm_ctx->lock);
+	if (err) {
+		pvr_vm_bind_op_fini(&bind_op);
+		return err;
+	}
 	err = drm_gpuvm_exec_lock(&vm_exec);
 	if (err)
 		goto err_cleanup;
